.TH RICE 1 "2026-07-26" "rice 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rice \- switch the whole desktop to a theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rice
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies a palette to every themed surface on the machine: terminal, editors,
status bar, file manager, browser and wallpaper. A theme is a directory under
\fIthemes/\fR holding a \fIpalette.toml\fR and a wallpaper. Rice writes theme
files and one pointer line per surface; it never rewrites a whole config.
.PP
Rice refuses to apply a palette containing the string TODO.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show available themes, one per line, with display name and variant.
.TP
.B use \fItheme\fR
Apply a theme to every surface.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RICE_HOME
Path to the rice repository. Defaults to \fI~/cc/rice\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dt (1),
.BR ghostty (1)
